  "facts": {
    "value": "The resident first reported concerns about a retaining fence in the property's garden in August 2022. The landlord inspected it and agreed that works needed to be done. However, works were delayed. She complained to the landlord on 21 May 2024 about a lack of progress. It apologised and paid her compensation. However, it still did not carry out the repairs. She complained to us in October 2024. The landlord carried out works on the fence in July 2025. The resident reports her concerns about a retaining wall at the property to the landlord on 20 August 2022. Between 6 September 2022 and 2 September 2024, the resident raised the issue of the retaining fence with the landlord on numerous occasions. It sent people out to inspect on several occasions but took no action as it did not know if it was responsible for maintaining it. On 21 April 2024, the resident complained to the landlord about its handling of her reports that her boundary fence was dangerously in need of repair. She pointed out that she was registered blind and so found the danger posed by the fence particularly worrying. On 18 July 2024, the landlord provided its stage 1 complaint response apologising for the late complaint response and delay in carrying out necessary works, offering £350 in compensation. On 20 July 2024, the resident asked to escalate her complaint to stage 2. On 21 August 2024, the landlord issued its stage 2 complaint response, increasing its compensation offer to £700 in total. On 25 October 2024, the resident asked us to investigate, saying her back garden was unsafe so she could not use it and the landlord had failed to address the problem adequately for over 3 years.",
